    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d593">

                <pb facs="1429" n="1413" xml:id="pg1413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.31/9–2051: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">GATT</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Delegation to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-09-20T23:00:00+01:00">September 20,
                            1951—11 p. m</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Tagg 17. From USDel
                    GATT. Cuban del GATT has not yet reed instrs re US proposal for severance GATT obligations with Czech. This matter extremely
                    urgent and plenary discussion probable Sat, Sept 22. Vargas<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d593-f1"/> has cabled but no reply. Pls do utmost obtain immediate
                    favorable instrs to Cuba del. Every vote counts.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d593-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Dept also pass Habana. Priority sent Habana 1, rptd info Dept Tagg 17.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d593-f1" n="1" xml:id="d593-f1-content">
                <p>Andres Vargas-Gomez, Special Adviser, Division of Economic Affairs, Cuban
                    Ministry of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d593-f2" n="2" xml:id="d593-f2-content">
                <p>On September 21 the following notation was inscribed on the action copy of this
                    cable by Carl D. Corse, Chief of the Commercial Policy Staff: “Called Duwayne
                    Clark [Counselor of Embassy in Cuba] saying it was completely accurate that
                    every vote did count and asking strongest representations to Cubans. He
                    indicated seeing F[oreign] O[ffice] this morning and will suggest Cubans cable
                    Vargas as well as call him. Clark will cable results to Geneva &amp; Dept.”</p>
                <p>The Embassy in Cuba reported at noontime, September 21 that the Embassy had been
                    informed that instructions had been prepared and would be sent that day to the
                    Cuban delegate at Geneva to “support and cooperate in every respect US proposal
                    for severance GATT obligations with
                    Czechoslovakia.” (Habana telegram 220, September 21, noon, 394.31/9–2151).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
